.\" Manual page for tr-shell. View with: man ./docs/trsh.1
.TH TRSH 1 "November 2026" "tr-shell 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trsh \- a Unix shell with Turkish commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trsh
.br
.B trsh
.I file
.RI [ argument ...]
.br
.B trsh \-c
.I command
.RI [ name
.RI [ argument ...]]
.br
.B trsh
.RB [ \-\-surum | \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-yardim | \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trsh
is an interactive command interpreter and scripting language whose
commands, keywords and messages are in Turkish.
Programs in
.B PATH
run as usual, so
.BR ls ,
.B git
and
.B gcc
work next to the Turkish commands.
.PP
Started on a terminal, the shell switches to the alternate screen, shows a
welcome box and a two\-line prompt with the directory, git branch, time and
the status of the last command.
When standard input is not a terminal, commands are read from it without a
prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I file
Run the script
.IR file .
Inside it,
.B $0
is the file name and
.BR $1 ", " $2 " ..."
are the arguments.
The exit status is that of the last command, or the code given to
.BR cikis .
.TP
.BI \-c " command"
Run
.I command
and exit.
The next argument, if given, becomes
.BR $0 ;
the rest become
.BR $1 " ..."
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-surum
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-yardim
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH SHELL SYNTAX
.TP
.B Quoting
Single quotes keep text literally; double quotes allow variables and
.BR $(...) ;
a backslash escapes the next character.
.TP
.B Lists
.IB a " ; " b
runs both,
.IB a " && " b
runs
.I b
if
.I a
succeeded,
.IB a " || " b
if it failed,
.IB a " &"
runs
.I a
in the background.
A line ending in
.BR | ,
.B &&
or
.B ||
continues on the next line.
.TP
.B Pipelines and redirection
.IB a " | " b
connects output to input.
Redirections are
.BR "< > >> 2> 2>> 2>&1" .
.TP
.B Expansion
.BR $NAME ,
.BR ${NAME} ,
.B $?
(last status),
.B $$
(shell PID),
.BR $0 \- $9 ,
.B $#
(argument count),
.B $@
(all arguments),
.B ~
(home directory),
.B $(command)
(its output) and the file name patterns
.BR * ,
.B ?
and
.BR [...] .
Unquoted
.B $(...)
and
.B $@
are split into words.
.B NAME=value
sets a variable; placed before a command it applies to that command only.
.TP
.B Comments
A
.B #
at the start of a word starts a comment that runs to the end of the line.
.SH CONTROL FLOW
Keywords are recognized only where a command starts and only when unquoted.
Blocks may be written on one line or across several, may be nested, and may
be redirected, piped or run in the background as a whole.
.TP
.BI "eger " condition " ise " commands " [degilse " commands "] son"
Runs the first
.I commands
if
.I condition
succeeds, otherwise the
.B degilse
part.
.B ise
may follow the condition without a separator.
.TP
.BI "dongu " condition " yap " commands " son"
Repeats
.I commands
while
.I condition
succeeds.
.TP
.BI "her " name " icin " words " yap " commands " son"
Runs
.I commands
once for each of the expanded
.IR words ,
with the variable
.I name
set to it.
.TP
.BR kir ", " devam
Leave the innermost loop, or go on to its next turn.
.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.B yardim
lists every command;
.BI "yardim " command
explains one.
The most important ones:
.TP
.BR listele ", " agac ", " oku ", " kopyala ", " tasi ", " klasor ", " olustur ", " sil ", " copkutusu
List, show, copy, move and create files.
.B sil
moves files to a trash in
.I ~/.trsh/cop
that
.B copkutusu
can restore from.
.TP
.BR gec ", " geri ", " ev ", " nerdeyim
Change to a directory, back to the previous one, or home; print the current one.
.TP
.BR sistem ", " surecler ", " oldur ", " disk ", " bellek ", " tarih ", " zamanla
System overview, processes, disk and memory use, date, and timing a command.
.TP
.BR hesapla ", " not ", " notlar
Calculator, and quick notes kept in
.IR ~/.trsh/notlar .
.TP
.BR isler ", " on ", " arka
List jobs, bring one to the foreground, continue one in the background.
.TP
.BR degisken ", " takmaad ", " takmaadsil ", " ayar ", " tema ", " gecmis
Variables, aliases, settings, color theme and history.
.TP
.BI "kaynak " file
Run
.I file
in the current shell, so its variables and aliases stay.
.TP
.BR cikis " [" \fIcode\fR "], " exit
Leave the shell.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Discard the line or open block being typed, or stop the running command
or loop.
The shell itself is never stopped.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z
Stop the running job;
.B isler
lists it and
.B on
or
.B arka
resumes it.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Leave the shell (on an empty line).
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Up ", " Down ", " Ctrl+R
Completion and history, when built with GNU readline.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.trsh/config
Settings
.RB ( tema ,
.BR isim ,
.BR karsilama ,
.BR gecmis_boyutu )
and a
.B [takmaad]
section with aliases.
.TP
.I ~/.trsh/baslangic
Commands run when an interactive shell starts.
.TP
.I ~/.trsh/history
Command history.
.TP
.I ~/.trsh/cop
Trash used by
.BR sil .
.TP
.I ~/.trsh/notlar
Notes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, no colors are used.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor opened by
.BR "ayar duzenle" .
.TP
.B HOME
Location of the
.I ~/.trsh
directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status of the last command run;
.B cikis
.I code
sets it explicitly.
A syntax error gives 2, a command that is not found 127, a file that cannot
be executed 126, and a command killed by signal
.I N
gives 128+\fIN\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
her dosya icin *.c yap
    echo "$dosya: $(oku $dosya | wc \-l) lines"
son

eger test \-f notlar.txt ise oku notlar.txt; degilse echo yok; son

trsh \-c 'echo $0 $1' name first
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR sh (1)
.PP
https://github.com/yusuffeness/tr\-shell
